<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
    <title>Valeriy Onuchin — Software Engineer</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fira+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
    <style>
        :root { --bg: #f7f8f8; --surface: #ffffff; --ink: #14181c; --ink-2: #48505a; --accent: #0e6f78; --sans: "Fira Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --bg: #0e1214; --surface: #151b1e; --ink: #eef1f3; --ink-2: #aab3bb; --accent: #62c6cc; } }
        body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink-2); font: 400 16px/1.6 var(--sans); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
        h1, h2, h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--ink); }
        p { margin: 0 0 1rem 0; }
        .page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 20px; }
        .profile { display: flex; gap: 2rem; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; }
        .portrait { width: 150px; height: 150px; border-radius: 50%; object-fit: cover; }
        h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; }
        .role { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
        .place { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.95rem; }
        .links { display: flex; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
        .links a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; }
        .links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
        .block { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
        .block h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; }
        .job { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
        .job h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
        .job .date { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
        .job p { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
        .job ul { margin: 0.5rem 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
        .job li { margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
        .skills { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr; gap: 10px; }
        .skills dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }
        @media (max-width: 600px) {
            .profile { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; gap: 1rem; }
            .skills { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
            .skills dd { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="page">
        <header class="profile">
            <img class="portrait" src="./images/me158.webp" alt="Valeriy Onuchin">
            <div>
                <h1>Valeriy Onuchin</h1>
                <p class="role">Senior Software Engineer</p>
                <p class="place">Protvino, Moscow region, Russia</p>
                <div class="links">
                    <a href="mailto:valeriy.onuchin@yandex.ru">Email</a>
                    <a href="https://github.com/x2v0" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
                    <a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3022-3529" target="_blank">ORCID</a>
                    <a href="https://www.scopus.com/authid/detail.uri?authorId=8401982000" target="_blank">Scopus</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </header>

        <main>
            <section class="block">
                <h2>About</h2>
                <p>Almost 40 years in research institutes and in industry. I know what physicists need from software, and how to build it so it keeps running for years.</p>
                <p>Co-author of <a href="https://root.cern" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent);">ROOT</a>, CERN's data analysis framework, which was used in the discovery of the Higgs boson. Twelve years of software for a proton therapy system. Most recently, Linux distributions and operating systems for x86_64, Elbrus and aarch64.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="block">
                <h2>Experience</h2>
                <div class="job">
                    <h3>Software Engineer</h3>
                    <div class="date">03.2025 – 12.2025 · ELVEES R&D Center</div>
                    <p>Altel OS, based on ALT Linux, for the Russian Elbrus-2000 and Skif (aarch64) platforms; cross-compilation.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>OS images for the Skif SoC (1892VA018, 4 × Cortex-A53): 8 variants, from build host and router to GNOME and KDE, Linux kernel 6.6.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="job">
                    <h3>Systems Programmer</h3>
                    <div class="date">2022 – 2024 · JINR, Dubna</div>
                    <p>Software for the SPD experiment at the NICA collider, Joint Institute for Nuclear Research.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Docker image for distributed computing: detector simulation and physics event reconstruction (Geant4, Pythia8, ROOT, Gaudi).</li>
                        <li>Automated from-source build of a Linux distribution: 170+ packages for x86_64, e2k and aarch64.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="job">
                    <h3>Lead Medical Software Developer</h3>
                    <div class="date">2009 – 2021 · Protom, Protvino</div>
                    <p>Software for proton cancer therapy: a 3D DICOM viewer, a patient video monitoring system, diagnostics, databases.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>3D CT viewer with contour and dose editing; converts DICOM into the treatment planning system’s format.</li>
                        <li>Patient position monitoring: live video is compared with a reference image.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="job">
                    <h3>Software Developer, ROOT team</h3>
                    <div class="date">2004 – 2008 · CERN, Geneva</div>
                    <p>Co-author of ROOT, the data analysis framework of high energy physics: more than 4 million lines of C++.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Windows GUI and graphics port of ROOT (TGWin32).</li>
                        <li>The signals and slots mechanism (TQObject, TQConnection).</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="block">
                <h2>Skills</h2>
                <dl class="skills">
                    <dt>Languages</dt><dd>C++, C#, Python, Go, Kotlin, bash, PowerShell</dd>
                    <dt>Build</dt><dd>CMake, Meson/Ninja, autotools, Make, msbuild, pkg-config</dd>
                    <dt>DevOps</dt><dd>Docker, CI/CD, cross-compilation, Linux kernel, OS builds</dd>
                    <dt>Platforms</dt><dd>Linux, Windows, Android, Elbrus-2000, Skif (aarch64)</dd>
                </dl>
            </section>
        </main>
    </div>

